{"Title":"An Act authorizing the reorientation and further lease of a parcel of land occupied by Riverside Boat Club of Cambridge","BillNumber":"S2923","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"S30","Name":"Senate Committee on Ways and Means","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S30","ResponseDate":"2024-07-31T10:34:35.687"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"SND0","Name":"Sal N. DiDomenico","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SND0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T14:24:30.23"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2923/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"Senate, July 31, 2024 -- The committee on Senate Ways and Means, to whom was referred the Senate Bill authorizing the reorientation of the parcel of land occupied by Riverside Boat Club of Cambridge (Senate, No. 1991),- reports, recommending that the same ought to pass with an amendment substituting a new draft entitled: \"An Act authorizing the reorientation and further lease of a parcel of land occupied by Riverside Boat Club of Cambridge\" (Senate, No. 2923).","DocumentText":"\tPursuant to chapter 65 of the acts of 2010 and notwithstanding section 5A of chapter 3 of the General Laws, the commissioner of capital asset management and maintenance, in consultation with the commissioner of conservation and recreation, may lease or enter into other agreements with Riverside Boat Club of Cambridge in the city of Cambridge, for a reconfigured parcel of land for the continued operation of its historical rowing program and boathouse. The parcel of land is more particularly described on a plan of land entitled “Plan Showing Reoriented Boundary for Riverside Boat Club of Cambridge”, revised July 29, 2024, including adjacent water sheet currently being used and shall include appurtenant rights of access from adjoining public roadways. The commissioner of capital asset management and maintenance may make minor revisions to the plan and file the same for recording in the Middlesex southern district registry of deeds and may execute any leases or other agreements consistent with said chapter 65.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable with Amendment","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H34","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H34"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H52","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H52"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Correctly Drawn","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H36","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H36"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[{"AmendmentNumber":"1","ParentBillNumber":"S2923","Branch":"House","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2923/Branches/House/Amendments/1/"}]}